        "original_id": "de29170e-6607-54e0-b8a4-df32f67ee654",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: William Bromley-Davenport, Arthur Balfour\n- Roles: Member of Parliament, Financial Secretary to the War Office, Prime Minister of the United Kingdom, Foreign Secretary\n- Topics: British politics, Conservative Party\n\nFacts:\n- Arthur Balfour was born on 25 July 1848 and died on 19 March 1930.\n- William Bromley-Davenport served as a Member of Parliament from 1886 to 1906.\n- Arthur Balfour was a British Conservative politician.\n- Arthur Balfour served as Prime Minister of the United Kingdom from July 1902 to December 1905.\n- Under Arthur Balfour, William Bromley-Davenport held the office of Financial Secretary to the War Office from 1903 to 1905.\n- Arthur Balfour later served as Foreign Secretary.",
